From: OpenAI Codex <codex@openai.com>
Subject: [PATCH] net: airoha: harden mailbox ownership and terminal teardown

Port the PR provider contract onto the current SoC and firmware loader.
Preserve named firmware images and upstream AN7583 support. Fold in the
minimal recovery, watchdog-lifetime, device-link and mailbox prerequisites
removed with the old upstream history; no SOE stack is restored.

Use bounded coherent mailbox slots, publish payloads before the doorbell,
check MMIO errors and retain ambiguous commands until a terminal reset.
Software BOOT_TRIGGER recovery is not an independently verified DMA fence:
never clear poisoned slots or reuse them during core recovery. A fresh-slot
health response restores FIFO mailbox liveness only.

Verify reset assertion before boot and terminal DMA release, and gate all
queue/IRQ accesses with the provider stop fence. Initialize locks before
IRQ registration and unwind IRQ/work, reset, buffers, then reserved pool.
On reset failure retain DMA rather than release firmware-owned memory.
Repeated terminal-stop attempts do not touch already stopped NPU MMIO.

The optional mailbox pool, consumer APIs and RCU access contract incorporate
the original provider-contract follow-up.

Signed-off-by: OpenAI Codex <codex@openai.com>
